  "system": {
    "description": "<p>A calling for one who would bring order to a land of chaos.</p><p></p><p>Knighthood once represented honor, courage, and self- sacrifice, and it stood for a bond greater than that of coin or blood. Knights were said to be benevolent and steadfast guardians of the commoners within their demesne. Today, warlords and petty criminals wear the title to satisfy their vanity and justify any number of imperious cruelties. While you may not have the holdings or share the virtues of knights past, you do share their most vital trait: you have an unbreakable determination, and you will not fall without a fight.</p>",
